    {
      "doc_type": "Invoice",
      "di_model": "prebuilt-invoice",
      "doc_notes": "This is a commercial invoice. The invoice body contains a MULTI-ROW product table — each row is a SEPARATE product. Extract each non-empty product row as a SEPARATE object in line_items. CRITICAL: never concatenate quantities from different rows into a single string or number. If row 1 has quantity 1716 and row 2 has quantity 910, produce TWO line_items entries — not '1716910'. Each line_item must have its own quantity, net_weight, gross_weight, item_description, and other per-row fields. Weight columns in the product table use metric tons (M/T) — e.g. '14.002560' means 14.002560 MT. Header summary lines (total packages, total net weight M/T, total gross weight M/T) go into key_value_pairs as gross_weight_total and net_weight_total respectively. Dates (invoice_date) must be ISO-8601 (YYYY-MM-DD).",
